Step 1: Install Axios

If you haven't already:

npm install axios
Step 2: Create db.json

Place this file in the root of your project (same place as package.json).

{
  "persons": [
    {
      "name": "Arto Hellas",
      "number": "040-123456",
      "id": "1"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ada Lovelace",
      "number": "39-44-5323523",
      "id": "2"
    },
    {
      "name": "Dan Abramov",
      "number": "12-43-234345",
      "id": "3"
    },
    {
      "name": "Mary Poppendieck",
      "number": "39-23-6423122",
      "id": "4"
    }
  ]
}
Step 3: Start the JSON Server

Run:

npx json-server --port 3001 db.json

You should see something like:

Resources
http://localhost:3001/persons

Open

http://localhost:3001/persons

in your browser.

If you see the JSON data, everything is working.

Step 4: Import Axios

At the top of App.jsx:

import axios from "axios";
Step 5: Import useEffect

Instead of

import { useState } from "react";

use

import { useState, useEffect } from "react";
Step 6: Remove the Hardcoded Persons

Delete this:

const [persons, setPersons] = useState([
  { name: "Arto Hellas", number: "040-123456" },
  { name: "Ada Lovelace", number: "39-44-5323523" },
  { name: "Dan Abramov", number: "12-43-234345" },
  { name: "Mary Poppendieck", number: "39-23-6423122" }
]);

Replace it with

const [persons, setPersons] = useState([]);

The array starts empty because the data will come from the server.

Step 7: Fetch the Data

Under your state declarations add:

useEffect(() => {
  axios.get("http://localhost:3001/persons")
    .then(response => {
      setPersons(response.data);
    });
}, []);

Your component will now:

Render.
Run the effect once.
Send a GET request to the server.
Receive the JSON.
Store it in persons.
Re-render with the fetched data.
Step 8: Your App Should Look Like This

Only the relevant part:

import { useState, useEffect } from "react";
import axios from "axios";

const App = () => {
  const [persons, setPersons] = useState([]);
  const [newName, setNewName] = useState("");
  const [newNumber, setNewNumber] = useState("");

  useEffect(() => {
    axios.get("http://localhost:3001/persons")
      .then(response => {
        setPersons(response.data);
      });
  }, []);

  // Rest of your code...
};